ent-ActionProperKungFuWolfDance = Wolf Dance
    .desc = Dash fast straight through a target up to 5 tiles away without bumping into it, stopping about a tile past it and staying on your feet. The target takes 20 Blunt to the body and is tossed into the air on the spot, landing knocked down (2 s stun). A held shield blocks the hit but gets knocked out of the hands. Right after a Claw Series the same dash hits much harder and sends the target further, only knocking them down; right after a Claw Whirlwind an even faster dash sends the target 5 tiles. You stay on your feet in every case. If a living target already had at least 85 damage, the plain dash turns into a finisher: 10 more fast dashes through the locked target, each turned 90 degrees (5 Blunt to the body and a toss each), then a final strike for 30 Slash to the head, torso, arms and legs that throws the target 7 tiles. Any Wolf Dance hit marks the target for the Hammer for 2 seconds. A finisher heals you for 25.
ent-ActionProperKungFuClawWhirlwind = Claw Whirlwind
    .desc = Throw a target within fist reach over yourself and meet their jaw with your knee (10 Blunt to the torso, broken skull, brain trauma). They slowly spin up into the air and crash down. The target can't move for about 2 seconds. Shields don't help. If a living target already had at least 80 damage, a huge ascending and then descending claw slash (90 Slash to the torso each) hits them in the air and slams them into the floor (knocked down 4 seconds). A Wolf Dance within 2 seconds becomes an even faster dash that sends the target 5 tiles away. Right after a Wolf Grip it becomes a two-handed cross strike instead of the throw.
ent-ActionProperKungFuHammer = Hammer
    .desc = One sweeping downward claw strike into the head of a target within fist reach (15 Blunt, eyes and brain lose 30 percent). The target is floored and can't get up for 5 seconds. Right after a Wolf Grip it deals 20 Blunt to the head and you backflip away, and a Wolf Dance within 2 seconds becomes an instant dash into the target. Within 2 seconds after a Wolf Dance hit it deals 20 Blunt to the body and sends the target exactly 5 tiles away. If a living target already had at least 80 damage, it becomes a finisher on the locked target: a light claw strike (1 damage), a straight strike (5 Blunt to the torso) that pushes them 2 tiles, a front flip into another strike (5 Blunt to the torso), and a spinning claw strike across the head (50 Blunt) that spins them sideways and lands them knocked down 5 tiles from you; the skull is never broken and the finisher heals you for 25. A target that was already lying takes 50 Blunt to the head and falls asleep for 30 seconds.
ent-ActionProperKungFuWolfInstinct = Wolf Instinct
    .desc = For 3 seconds you take a counter stance. Every melee attack on you is parried and answered with a two-palm strike into the attacker's chest (25 Slash, 75 stamina damage); they fly back 3 tiles but stay on their feet. If a gun hurts you, you dash at the shooter up to 8 tiles and, if you reach them, knock them down, knock the gun out of their hands and take them into a hard grab without hurting them; a shooter further away is missed. Thrown objects don't hurt you and fly back at the thrower twice as fast.
ent-ActionProperKungFuWolfPack = Wolf Pack
    .desc = Call 1 to 3 wolves in your own image out of white-red smoke around you for 30 seconds. They wear harmless copies of your clothes, know Proper Kung Fu, have 20 health and deal half damage. They go for the chosen target, for whoever attacks you and for whoever you attack, and never touch you or each other. When slain or when time runs out they vanish in red smoke and leave nothing behind.
ent-ActionProperKungFuKunai = Kunai
    .desc = Summon a kunai into your hand out of white-red smoke. It cuts like a combat knife (15 Slash). Thrown, it sticks into whatever it hits (15 Slash to a body), and wherever it lands or sticks you teleport to it in a puff of smoke and the kunai is gone. Only one summoned kunai exists at a time; an unused one fades after 60 seconds. Allowed despite the ban on ranged weapons.
ent-ActionProperKungFuJoinPack = Join the Pack
    .desc = Spend 10 seconds teaching another person next to you. Moving or taking damage interrupts it. They learn Proper Kung Fu (pupil) - Claw Series, Wolf Grip and a torso-only Perfect Flow - with the same damage but weaker effects and none of the skills, passives, finishers, synergies or the ultimate; unlike the master, they can still use guns. Does not work on someone who already knows a martial art.
